# ULX demo and docs: no new i18n for copy

**`src/locales/en-us.js` is for the published addon** (keys used under `src/` at runtime). **Demos and documentation are not allowed to grow that file** or introduce translation keys for doc-only wording.

## Do

- Use **plain string literals** in templates and JS for demo titles, placeholders, `aria-label`, snippet text, notices, and example copy (`"Save"`, `{{"Example"}}`, `@description="..."`, etc.).
- When updating demos or snippets, **never add keys to `src/locales/en-us.js`** just to localize demo text.

## Do not

- Add **`t("…")`** calls in `ulx/src/demo/ulx-ember/` for strings that exist **only** in demos/docs (that would imply new locale entries).
- Add or request **new message keys** in `en-us.js` for demonstration or documentation purposes.

## Rare exception

Using **`t(...)` only when deliberately exercising an existing addon key** already present in **`src/locales/en-us.js`** (e.g. proving a shipped default label). If in doubt, **inline English** instead of expanding the addon locale.
